21:48:19 said  I built Cue Player, a Linux video-only player with a typed `HH:MM:SS` start cue, cue nudging, scrub preview, file browser, drag-and-drop, and Play/Stop control of Audacity through its scripting pipe. Playback uses bundled ffmpeg for broad format support, and the finished 56 MB x86_64 AppImage has passed both the screenshot and self-test checks. Stop rewinds the picture to the cue, and the interface adapts down to a compact window width. I verified the pipe commands against Audacity 3.7.7; Audacity 4.0 was not installed, so its command compatibility is the main unknown, and video is capped at 7…
