23:26:53 out   # Cue Player mechanics
23:26:53 out   This sheet lists the values that shape how Cue Player behaves. There is no
23:26:53 out   original program to compare against for this build, so every value below is
23:26:53 out   **estimated** from the request and from how Audacity 4.0's Space shortcut
23:26:53 out   behaves on the development machine. The same values live in
23:26:53 out   [`mechanics.json`](mechanics.json).
23:26:53 out   Cue Player is a video player, not a game. "Mechanics" here means playback,
23:26:53 out   cueing, the Audacity hand-off and the interface timings that affect them.
23:26:53 out   ## Playback
23:26:53 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
23:26:53 out   | --- | --- | --- |
23:26:53 out   | Playback rate | `1.0x` (the play head advances by the frame delta) | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Output frame rate | `30 fps` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Maximum decoded width | `1280 px` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Maximum decoded height | `720 px` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Decoded frame queue | `12 frames` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Decoder channel buffer | `8 frames` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Longest accepted frame step | `0.1 s` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   Frames are decoded by `ffmpeg` to raw RGBA, scaled with bicubic filtering to fit
23:26:53 out   inside 1280x720 while preserving aspect ratio, and sampled at a fixed 30 fps.
23:26:53 out   The player displays the newest frame whose timestamp has been reached, so a slow
23:26:53 out   decode skips frames instead of slowing playback. The image is letterboxed in the
23:26:53 out   window; it is never stretched.
23:26:53 out   Audio, subtitles and data streams are explicitly dropped (`-an -sn -dn`). Video
23:26:53 out   codecs and containers are whatever the bundled/system `ffmpeg` can decode:
23:26:53 out   MP4, MKV, MOV, WebM, AVI, MPEG, TS, MTS, OGV, FLV, WMV and more.
23:26:53 out   ## Start cue
23:26:53 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
23:26:53 out   | --- | --- | --- |
23:26:53 out   | Default start cue | `0 s` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Cue nudge | `1 s` (`-1s` / `+1s`) | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Large cue nudge | `10 s` (`-10s` / `+10s`) | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Arrow seek step | `5 s` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Cue input format | `hours:minutes:seconds` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   The start field accepts `HH:MM:SS`, `MM:SS`, or plain seconds and also accepts
23:26:53 out   fractional seconds (`00:01:02.500`). The value is clamped to `0..duration`.
23:26:53 out   Pressing Enter or clicking away commits it; Escape restores the previous cue.
23:26:53 out   The same cue is used in three places:
23:26:53 out   1. **Stop** rewinds the picture to the cue, so the next take starts from the same
23:26:53 out   frame.
23:26:53 out   2. **Play** after the clip has ended restarts from the cue.
23:26:53 out   3. The cue is drawn on the scrub bar as a bright marker, separate from the play
23:26:53 out   head.
23:26:53 out   The scrub bar is only a preview tool. Dragging it moves the picture and clock,
23:26:53 out   but it does not change the typed start cue. Use **Use playhead** to copy the
23:26:53 out   current scrub position into the cue.
23:26:53 out   ## Audacity hand-off
23:26:53 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
23:26:53 out   | --- | --- | --- |
23:26:53 out   | Play key | `Space` | verified against Audacity 4.0.1 |
23:26:53 out   | Stop key | `Space` | verified against Audacity 4.0.1 |
23:26:53 out   | Sync enabled by default | `true` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Audacity window poll interval | `2.0 s` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   When **AUDACITY TRANSPORT** is on, pressing Play or Stop finds the Audacity 4.0
23:26:53 out   window, focuses it for a moment, taps Space (Audacity's default Play/Stop
23:26:53 out   shortcut) through XTest, then returns focus to Cue Player. There is deliberately
23:26:53 out   no timeline synchronization: line up the start cue in Cue Player with the
23:26:53 out   Audacity play head by hand, then start from either side. Stop is sent even when
23:26:53 out   the video had already reached its end, so the audio transport cannot keep
23:26:53 out   running after the picture stops.
23:26:53 out   The Audacity window is re-checked every 2 seconds and the chip reads **keyboard
23:26:53 out   ready** when it is found. If Audacity is not running, or the X11 keyboard
23:26:53 out   libraries are unavailable, an error is shown once per session as a toast. The
23:26:53 out   hand-off uses X11, so a native Wayland session is not supported.
23:26:53 out   ## Controls and interface
23:26:53 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
23:26:53 out   | --- | --- | --- |
23:26:53 out   | Window size | `1180x760` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Toast duration | `4.5 s` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | File browser double-click window | `0.38 s` | estimated |
23:26:53 out   | Input | Action |
23:26:53 out   | --- | --- |
23:26:53 out   | Space | Play / Stop (Stop returns to the cue) |
23:26:53 out   | Escape | Stop and return to the cue |
23:26:53 out   | Enter (in start field) | Apply the typed start cue |
23:26:53 out   | Escape (in start field) | Discard the edit |
23:26:53 out   | Left / Right | Seek 5 seconds |
23:26:53 out   | Home | Jump to the cue |
23:26:53 out   | O | Open the file browser |
23:26:53 out   | F | Toggle fullscreen |
23:26:53 out   | Drag the scrub bar | Preview a position, keep playing/paused state |
23:26:53 out   | Drop a file on the window | Open it |
23:26:53 out   The layout switches to a compact transport below 820 px wide: the clock is
23:26:53 out   smaller, the Audacity chip is narrower and the cue buttons are tighter, so
23:26:53 out   nothing runs outside the panel.
23:26:53 out   ## Sources and unknowns
23:26:53 out   - The request defines the behaviour: Play/Stop control Audacity, typed start
23:26:53 out   point, video only, broad format support, AppImage.
23:26:53 out   - Audacity 4.0.1 on this machine responds to an injected Space key with its
23:26:53 out   `playback/toggle-play-stop` action. The hand-off uses X11/XTest, so native
23:26:53 out   Wayland is not covered.
23:26:53 out   - Every numeric value is a design choice for this build, not a copied constant.
23:26:53 out   - Decode size and frame rate trade sharpness for CPU and memory; they can be
23:26:53 out   changed in `src/player.rs` and kept in step with `mechanics.json`.
23:26:53 out   #!/usr/bin/env bash
23:26:53 out   # Build a self-contained Cue Player AppImage.
23:26:53 out   #
23:26:53 out   # ./scripts/build-appimage.sh
23:26:53 out   #
23:26:53 out   # It downloads a static ffmpeg/ffprobe build and appimagetool into build/cache
23:26:53 out   # the first time, stages build/CuePlayer.AppDir, and writes dist/*.AppImage.
23:26:53 out   # No FUSE is needed: the tool is run with APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1.
23:26:53 out   set -euo pipefail
23:26:53 out   ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)"
23:26:53 out   cd "$ROOT"
23:26:53 out   APP="CuePlayer"
23:26:53 out   ARCH="${ARCH:-x86_64}"
23:26:53 out   VERSION="$(sed -n 's/^version = "\(.*\)"/\1/p' Cargo.toml | head -n 1)"
23:26:53 out   if [ -z "$VERSION" ]; then
23:26:53 out   echo "Could not read the version from Cargo.toml" >&2
23:26:53 out   exit 1
23:26:53 out   fi
23:26:53 out   case "$ARCH" in
23:26:53 out   x86_64)
23:26:53 out   FFMPEG_URL="https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/releases/ffmpeg-release-amd64-static.tar.xz"
23:26:53 out   APPIMAGETOOL_URL="https://github.com/AppImage/appimagetool/releases/download/continuous/appimagetool-x86_64.AppImage"
23:26:53 out   ;;
23:26:53 out   *)
23:26:53 out   echo "Only x86_64 AppImages are supported by this script (got ARCH=$ARCH)." >&2
23:26:53 out   echo "Set ARCH=x86_64 or adapt the download URLs." >&2
23:26:53 out   exit 1
23:26:53 out   ;;
23:26:53 out   esac
23:26:53 out   BUILD="$ROOT/build"
23:26:53 out   CACHE="$BUILD/cache"
23:26:53 out   APPDIR="$BUILD/$APP.AppDir"
23:26:53 out   DIST="$ROOT/dist"
23:26:53 out   BIN="$ROOT/target/release/cue-video-player"
23:26:53 out   FF_DIR="$CACHE/ffmpeg-static"
23:26:53 out   FF_ARCHIVE="$CACHE/ffmpeg-static.tar.xz"
23:26:53 out   APPIMAGETOOL="$CACHE/appimagetool-$ARCH.AppImage"
23:26:53 out   OUT="$DIST/$APP-$VERSION-$ARCH.AppImage"
23:26:53 out   need() {
23:26:53 out   command -v "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
23:26:53 out   echo "Missing required command: $1" >&2
23:26:53 out   exit 1
23:26:53 out   }
23:26:53 out   }
23:26:53 out   need cargo
23:26:53 out   need curl
23:26:53 out   need tar
23:26:53 out   need xz
23:26:53 out   echo "==> Building release binary"
23:26:53 out   cargo build --release --locked
23:26:53 out   echo "==> Preparing build folders"
23:26:53 out   mkdir -p "$CACHE" "$DIST"
23:26:53 out   rm -rf "$APPDIR"
23:26:53 out   mkdir -p "$APPDIR/usr/bin" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPDIR/usr/share/applications" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPDIR/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPDIR/usr/share/doc/cue-player"
23:26:53 out   echo "==> Fetching static ffmpeg and ffprobe (cached)"
23:26:53 out   if [ ! -x "$FF_DIR/ffmpeg" ] || [ ! -x "$FF_DIR/ffprobe" ]; then
23:26:53 out   if [ ! -f "$FF_ARCHIVE" ]; then
23:26:53 out   curl -fL --retry 3 --retry-delay 2 -o "$FF_ARCHIVE" "$FFMPEG_URL"
23:26:53 out   fi
23:26:53 out   rm -rf "$FF_DIR"
23:26:53 out   mkdir -p "$FF_DIR"
23:26:53 out   tar -xJf "$FF_ARCHIVE" -C "$FF_DIR" --strip-components=1
23:26:53 out   fi
23:26:53 out   echo "==> Fetching appimagetool (cached)"
23:26:53 out   if [ ! -x "$APPIMAGETOOL" ]; then
23:26:53 out   if [ ! -f "$APPIMAGETOOL" ]; then
23:26:53 out   curl -fL --retry 3 --retry-delay 2 -o "$APPIMAGETOOL" "$APPIMAGETOOL_URL"
23:26:53 out   fi
23:26:53 out   chmod +x "$APPIMAGETOOL"
23:26:53 out   fi
23:26:53 out   echo "==> Staging AppDir"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm755 "$BIN" "$APPDIR/usr/bin/cue-video-player"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm755 "$FF_DIR/ffmpeg" "$APPDIR/usr/bin/ffmpeg"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm755 "$FF_DIR/ffprobe" "$APPDIR/usr/bin/ffprobe"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm644 "$ROOT/assets/cue-player.png" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPDIR/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/cue-player.png"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm644 "$ROOT/scripts/cue-player.desktop" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPDIR/usr/share/applications/cue-player.desktop"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm644 "$ROOT/README.md" "$APPDIR/usr/share/doc/cue-player/README.md"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm644 "$ROOT/MECHANICS.md" "$APPDIR/usr/share/doc/cue-player/MECHANICS.md"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm644 "$ROOT/LICENSE" "$APPDIR/usr/share/doc/cue-player/LICENSE"
23:26:53 out   install -Dm644 "$ROOT/assets/fonts/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPDIR/usr/share/doc/cue-player/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt"
23:26:53 out   cp "$APPDIR/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/cue-player.png" "$APPDIR/cue-player.png"
23:26:53 out   cp "$APPDIR/usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/cue-player.png" "$APPDIR/.DirIcon"
23:26:53 out   cp "$APPDIR/usr/share/applications/cue-player.desktop" "$APPDIR/cue-player.desktop"
23:26:53 out   cat > "$APPDIR/AppRun" <<'APPRUN'
23:26:53 out   #!/bin/sh
23:26:53 out   # AppRun for Cue Player. Keep ffmpeg and ffprobe next to the binary.
23:26:53 out   set -eu
23:26:53 out   HERE="$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)"
23:26:53 out   export APPDIR="$HERE"
23:26:53 out   export PATH="$HERE/usr/bin:${PATH:-/usr/bin:/bin}"
23:26:53 out   exec "$HERE/usr/bin/cue-video-player" "$@"
23:26:53 out   APPRUN
23:26:53 out   chmod +x "$APPDIR/AppRun"
23:26:53 out   if command -v desktop-file-validate >/dev/null 2>&1; then
23:26:53 out   desktop-file-validate "$APPDIR/usr/share/applications/cue-player.desktop" || true
23:26:53 out   fi
23:26:53 out   echo "==> Packing AppImage"
23:26:53 out   rm -f "$OUT"
23:26:53 out   APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1 ARCH="$ARCH" \
23:26:53 out   "$APPIMAGETOOL" --no-appstream "$APPDIR" "$OUT"
23:26:53 out   chmod +x "$OUT"
23:26:53 out   echo
23:26:53 out   echo "Built $OUT"
23:26:53 out   ls -lh "$OUT"
23:26:53 out   #!/usr/bin/env python3
23:26:53 out   """Draw the Cue Player app icon.
23:26:53 out   Run from the app folder: python3 scripts/make-icon.py
23:26:53 out   Requires Pillow. The committed PNG is used by the AppImage build; this script
23:26:53 out   exists so the icon can be regenerated or recoloured later.
23:26:53 out   """
23:26:53 out   from pathlib import Path
23:26:53 out   from PIL import Image, ImageDraw
23:26:53 out   ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
23:26:53 out   OUT = ROOT / "assets" / "cue-player.png"
23:26:53 out   BG = (11, 13, 16, 255)
23:26:53 out   PANEL = (28, 32, 39, 255)
23:26:53 out   AMBER = (230, 165, 74, 255)
23:26:53 out   BRIGHT = (248, 186, 94, 255)
23:26:53 out   DARK = (20, 17, 12, 255)
23:26:53 out   def build(size: int) -> Image.Image:
23:26:53 out   s = size / 512.0
23:26:53 out   def r(*values):
23:26:53 out   return tuple(round(v * s) for v in values)
23:26:53 out   img = Image.new("RGBA", (size, size), (0, 0, 0, 0))
23:26:53 out   d = ImageDraw.Draw(img)
23:26:53 out   d.rounded_rectangle(r(12, 12, 500, 500), radius=r(112)[0], fill=BG,
23:26:53 out   outline=AMBER, width=max(1, r(9)[0]))
23:26:53 out   # Film strip holes along the top and bottom.
23:26:53 out   for x in (92, 172, 252, 332, 412):
23:26:53 out   d.rounded_rectangle(r(x, 56, x + 36, 82), radius=r(6)[0], fill=PANEL)
23:26:53 out   d.rounded_rectangle(r(x, 430, x + 36, 456), radius=r(6)[0], fill=PANEL)
23:26:53 out   # Amber play mark.
23:26:53 out   d.polygon(
23:26:53 out   [r(198, 150), r(198, 362), r(372, 256)],
23:26:53 out   fill=AMBER,
23:26:53 out   )
23:26:53 out   d.polygon(
23:26:53 out   [r(216, 188), r(216, 324), r(328, 256)],
23:26:53 out   fill=BRIGHT,
23:26:53 out   )
23:26:53 out   # Dark pupil in the play mark keeps it from looking like a solid wedge.
23:26:53 out   d.polygon(
23:26:53 out   [r(212, 192), r(212, 320), r(318, 256)],
23:26:53 out   fill=DARK,
23:26:53 out   )
23:26:53 out   return img
23:26:53 out   def main() -> None:
23:26:53 out   OUT.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
23:26:53 out   build(512).resize((256, 256), Image.LANCZOS).save(OUT)
23:26:53 out   print(f"wrote {OUT}")
23:26:53 out   if __name__ == "__main__":
23:26:53 out   main()
