02:41:51 out   ## Start cue
02:41:51 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
02:41:51 out   | --- | --- | --- |
02:41:51 out   | Default start cue | `0 s` | estimated |
02:41:51 out   | Cue nudge | `1 s` (`-1s` / `+1s`) | estimated |
02:41:51 out   | Large cue nudge | `10 s` (`-10s` / `+10s`) | estimated |
02:41:51 out   | Arrow seek step | `5 s` | estimated |
02:41:51 out   | Cue input format | `hours:minutes:seconds.milliseconds` | user request |
02:41:51 out   | Default cue text | `00:00:00.000` | user request |
02:41:51 out   | Start-field font | `16 px` normal, `14 px` compact, `13 px` narrow | estimated |
02:41:51 out   | Start-field width | `160 px` normal, `144 px` compact, `130 px` narrow | estimated |
02:41:51 out   The start field accepts `HH:MM:SS.mmm` (for example `00:01:23.500`), and also
02:41:51 out   `HH:MM:SS`, `MM:SS`, or plain seconds. Fractional seconds are parsed from the
02:41:51 out   part after the decimal point. The value is clamped to `0..duration`.
02:41:51 out   Pressing Enter or clicking away commits it; Escape restores the previous cue.
02:41:51 out   The same cue is used in three places:
02:41:51 out   1. **Stop** rewinds the picture to the cue, so the next take starts from the same
02:41:51 out   frame.
02:41:51 out   2. **Play** after the clip has ended restarts from the cue.
02:41:51 out   3. The cue is drawn on the scrub bar as a bright marker, separate from the play
02:41:51 out   head.
02:41:51 out   The scrub bar is only a preview tool. Dragging it moves the picture and clock,
02:41:51 out   but it does not change the typed start cue. Use **Use playhead** to copy the
02:41:51 out   current scrub position into the cue. In the narrowest layout the `-10s` and
02:41:51 out   `+10s` buttons are hidden so the field and single-second nudges still fit.
02:41:51 out   ## Audacity hand-off
02:41:51 out   | Value | Setting | Source |
