14:42:45 out   The start field accepts `HH:MM:SS.mmm` (for example `00:01:23.500`), and also
14:42:45 out   `HH:MM:SS`, `MM:SS`, or plain seconds. Fractional seconds are parsed from the
14:42:45 out   part after the decimal point. The value is clamped to `0..duration`.
14:42:45 out   Pressing Enter or clicking away commits it; Escape restores the previous cue.
14:42:45 out   The same cue is used in three places:
14:42:45 out   1. **Stop** rewinds the picture to the cue, so the next take starts from the same
14:42:45 out   frame.
14:42:45 out   2. **Play** after the clip has ended restarts from the cue.
14:42:45 out   3. The cue is drawn on the scrub bar as a bright marker, separate from the play
14:42:45 out   head.
14:42:45 out   The scrub bar is only a preview tool. Dragging it moves the picture and clock,
14:42:45 out   but it does not change the typed start cue. Use **Use playhead** to copy the
14:42:45 out   current scrub position into the cue. There are no cue nudge buttons; the arrow
14:42:45 out   keys seek 5 seconds at a time.
