16:02:45 out   ## Known limits
16:02:45 out   - Frame-accurate seeking depends on keyframes and on `ffmpeg`'s input seeking;
16:02:45 out   the typed cue is accurate to about a frame, not sample-accurate.
16:02:45 out   - Video is capped at 1280x720 and 30 fps to keep decode affordable. The cap can
16:02:45 out   be raised in `src/player.rs` (and in `mechanics.json`).
16:02:45 out   - Audacity 4.0's transport is driven by its Space, P and R shortcuts, so
16:02:45 out   Audacity must be running on an X11 desktop and its main window must be open.
16:02:45 out   Native Wayland is not supported.
16:02:45 out   - The dark/light choice and accent colour are kept for the running session; they
16:02:45 out   reset to dark and purple when VidCue is restarted.
16:02:45 out   - The AppImage is built on x86_64; other architectures need their own static
16:02:45 out   ffmpeg and appimagetool build.
