01:03:58 out   ## Known limits
01:03:58 out   - The desktop accessibility bus must be available. VidCue can switch it on, but
01:03:58 out   it cannot create one where none is installed.
01:03:58 out   - Audacity 4.0.2 on Linux is the version observed while building. The accessible
01:03:58 out   object name used here is `Playback position:00 h 00 m 00.000 s`; a future
01:03:58 out   Audacity release could rename it.
01:03:58 out   - Audacity's stop action returns its play head to the start of the selection or
01:03:58 out   project; VidCue follows that position, so the picture returns with it.
01:03:58 out   - Frame-accurate seeking depends on keyframes and on `ffmpeg`'s input seeking;
01:03:58 out   the picture is accurate to about a frame, not sample-accurate.
01:03:58 out   - Video is capped at 1280x720 and 30 fps to keep decode affordable. The cap can
01:03:58 out   be raised in `src/player.rs` (and in `mechanics.json`).
01:03:58 out   Audacity and its `00h00m00.000s` display, a minimalist slave player, and
01:03:58 out   window-order independence.
01:03:58 out   - Audacity 4.0.2 was running on the build machine. Its accessible tree exposes
01:03:58 out   the name `Playback position:00 h 00 m 00.000 s`, and the value advanced while
01:03:58 out   Audacity played. VidCue's live trace followed it and reset with Audacity's
01:03:58 out   stop-to-zero.
01:03:58 out   - Audacity 4.0 on other Linux desktops, and any future Audacity version, could
01:03:58 out   expose a different accessible name. That is the main remaining unknown.
01:03:58 out   - The accessibility bus must be running. VidCue switches `IsEnabled` on, but
01:03:58 out   cannot install a missing AT-SPI stack.
01:03:58 out   - Every numeric layout value is a design choice for this build, not a copied
01:03:58 out   constant.
01:03:58 out   - Decode size and frame rate trade sharpness for CPU and memory; they can be
01:03:58 out   changed in `src/player.rs` and kept in step with `mechanics.json`.
