01:40:51 out   - **Video only.** Audio, subtitle and data streams are dropped during decode.
01:40:51 out   - **Most formats.** Decoding is delegated to `ffmpeg`, so MP4, MKV, MOV, WebM,
01:40:51 out   AVI, MPEG, TS, MTS, OGV, FLV, WMV and other common containers work as long as
01:40:51 out   the bundled or system `ffmpeg` supports them.
01:40:51 out   - **Minimal interface.** A compact header, the picture, and one status bar.
01:40:51 out   There is no timecode entry field and no transport strip.
01:40:51 out   - **Optional appearance settings.** The gear still offers Dark / Light and six
01:40:51 out   accent colours: orange, yellow, green, blue, purple and red. Dark and purple
01:40:51 out   are the defaults.
01:40:51 out   - **File browser and drag-and-drop.** No GTK dialogs are needed.
01:40:51 out   - **Ships as an AppImage** with `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` inside, so the target machine
01:40:51 out   does not need ffmpeg installed.
01:40:51 out   ## Build and run
01:40:51 out   cargo run
01:40:51 out   cargo build
01:40:51 out   cargo test
01:40:51 out   ```
01:40:51 out   The app looks for `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` next to its executable first, then on
01:40:51 out   `PATH`. Override them with `CUE_FFMPEG` and `CUE_FFPROBE` if needed.
01:40:51 out   ## Connecting Audacity 4.0
01:40:51 out   - Audacity's stop action returns its play head to the start of the selection or
01:40:51 out   project; VIDSYNC follows that position, so the picture returns with it.
01:40:51 out   - Frame-accurate seeking depends on keyframes and on `ffmpeg`'s input seeking;
01:40:51 out   the picture is accurate to about a frame, not sample-accurate.
01:40:51 out   - Video is capped at 1280x720 and 30 fps to keep decode affordable. The cap can
01:40:51 out   be raised in `src/player.rs` (and in `mechanics.json`).
01:40:51 out   - The dark/light choice and accent colour are kept for the running session; they
01:40:51 out   reset to dark and purple when VIDSYNC is restarted.
01:40:51 out   - The AppImage is built on x86_64; other architectures need their own static
01:40:51 out   ffmpeg and appimagetool build.
