17:46:28 out   140:## Sources and unknowns
17:46:28 out   141-
17:46:28 out   142-- The latest request defines this version: no transport buttons, no start-time
17:46:28 out   143- field, no Audacity switch, a live `00:00:00.000` readout, a green/red dot for
17:46:28 out   144- Audacity and its `00h00m00.000s` display, a minimalist slave player, and
17:46:28 out   145- window-order independence.
17:46:28 out   146-- Audacity 4.0.2 was running on the build machine. Its accessible tree exposes
17:46:28 out   147- the name `Playback position:00 h 00 m 00.000 s`, and the value advanced while
17:46:28 out   148- Audacity played. VIDSYNC's live trace followed it and reset with Audacity's
17:46:28 out   149- stop-to-zero.
17:46:28 out   150-- Audacity 4.0 on other Linux desktops, and any future Audacity version, could
17:46:28 out   151- expose a different accessible name. VIDSYNC falls back to any short accessible
17:46:28 out   152- name that ends in a clock, so translated labels work, but a future release
17:46:28 out   153- could change the clock format itself.
17:46:28 out   154-- The accessibility bus must be running. VIDSYNC switches `IsEnabled` on, but
17:46:28 out   155- cannot install a missing AT-SPI stack.
17:46:28 out   156-- Every numeric layout value is a design choice for this build, not a copied
17:46:28 out   157- constant.
17:46:28 out   158-- Decode size and frame rate trade sharpness for CPU and memory; they can be
17:46:28 out   159- changed in `src/player.rs` and kept in step with `mechanics.json`.
