17:57:58 out   The layout switches to a compact status bar below 880 px wide: the bars get
17:57:58 out   shorter, the timecode drops to 22 px, the Audacity label drops to 12 px and the
17:57:58 out   side padding shrinks. Below 500 px the timecode drops to 18 px and its area
17:57:58 out   narrows to 160 px. The built-in file browser also drops its sidebar below
17:57:58 out   540 px and uses a smaller footer.
17:57:58 out   The gear opens an appearance popover rather than a separate settings window. A
17:57:58 out   Dark / Light choice switches the whole interface; dark is the default. Choosing
17:57:58 out   a swatch changes every accent immediately: the brand mark, play icon, settings
17:57:58 out   highlights and folder highlights. Both choices are saved to
17:57:58 out   `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vidsync/settings.json` and restored on the next launch, so a
17:57:58 out   missing file simply means dark and purple.
17:57:58 out   ## Sources and unknowns
17:57:58 out   - The latest request defines this version: no transport buttons, no start-time
17:57:58 out   field, no Audacity switch, a live `00:00:00.000` readout, a green/red dot for
17:57:58 out   Audacity and its `00h00m00.000s` display, a minimalist slave player, and
17:57:58 out   window-order independence.
17:57:58 out   - Audacity 4.0.2 was running on the build machine. Its accessible tree exposes
17:57:58 out   the name `Playback position:00 h 00 m 00.000 s`, and the value advanced while
17:57:58 out   Audacity played. VIDSYNC's live trace followed it and reset with Audacity's
17:57:58 out   stop-to-zero.
17:57:58 out   - Audacity 4.0 on other Linux desktops, and any future Audacity version, could
17:57:58 out   expose a different accessible name. VIDSYNC falls back to any short accessible
17:57:58 out   name that ends in a clock, so translated labels work, but a future release
17:57:58 out   could change the clock format itself.
17:57:58 out   - The accessibility bus must be running. VIDSYNC switches `IsEnabled` on, but
17:57:58 out   cannot install a missing AT-SPI stack.
17:57:58 out   - Every numeric layout value is a design choice for this build, not a copied
17:57:58 out   constant.
17:57:58 out   - Decode size and frame rate trade sharpness for CPU and memory; they can be
17:57:58 out   changed in `src/player.rs` and kept in step with `mechanics.json`.
