02:18:32 out   - **Minimal interface.** A compact header, the picture, and one status bar.
02:18:32 out   The picture runs edge-to-edge between the header and the status bar, with
02:18:32 out   black letterbox or pillarbox bars protecting its aspect ratio. There is no
02:18:32 out   timecode entry field and no transport strip.
02:18:32 out   -- **Optional appearance settings.** The gear offers Dark / Light and six accent
02:18:32 out   - colours: orange, yellow, green, blue, purple and red. Dark and purple are the
02:18:32 out   - defaults, and the chosen mode and colour are remembered on the next launch.
02:18:32 out   - The menu, desktop and window icons use the same purple play tile shown beside
02:18:32 out   - the name.
02:18:32 out   -- **File browser and drag-and-drop.** No GTK dialogs are needed.
02:18:32 out   +- **Optional appearance and window settings.** The gear offers Dark / Light,
02:18:32 out   + six accent colours (orange, yellow, green, blue, purple and red), and a
02:18:32 out   + **Keep on top** switch that holds the player above other windows. Dark,
02:18:32 out   + purple and off are the defaults, and all three choices are remembered on the
02:18:32 out   + next launch. The menu, desktop and window icons use the same purple play tile
02:18:32 out   + shown beside the name.
02:18:32 out   +- **File browser only.** Videos are opened from the built-in browser. There is
02:18:32 out   + no drag-and-drop target, no sample-clip shortcut and no empty-stage prompt;
02:18:32 out   + when nothing is loaded the picture area stays black. No GTK dialogs are
02:18:32 out   + needed.
02:18:32 out   - **Ships as an AppImage** with `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` inside, so the target machine
02:18:32 out   does not need ffmpeg installed.
02:18:32 out   ## Build and run
