02:28:25 out   # VIDSYNC mechanics
02:28:25 out   This sheet lists the values that shape VIDSYNC. There is no original program to
02:28:25 out   compare against, so design choices are marked **estimated**. Values taken from
02:28:25 out   the person's requests are marked with that source; values read from Audacity on
02:28:25 out   the build machine are marked **observed**. The same values live in
02:28:25 out   [`mechanics.json`](mechanics.json).
02:28:25 out   VIDSYNC is a video player, not a game. "Mechanics" here means following
02:28:25 out   Audacity 4.0's timecode, playback, the status bar and the small appearance
02:28:25 out   panel.
02:28:25 out   ## Following Audacity
02:28:25 out   The person asked for a player with no transport of its own: Audacity 4.0's
02:28:25 out   timecode is the clock, the player is the slave, and the hierarchy of desktop
02:28:25 out   The layout switches to a compact status bar below 880 px wide: the bars get
02:28:25 out   shorter, the timecode drops to 22 px, the Audacity label drops to 12 px and the
02:28:25 out   side padding shrinks. Below 500 px the timecode drops to 18 px and its area
02:28:25 out   narrows to 160 px. The built-in file browser also drops its sidebar below
02:28:25 out   540 px and uses a smaller footer.
02:28:25 out   The gear opens an appearance popover rather than a separate settings window. A
02:28:25 out   Dark / Light choice switches the whole interface; dark is the default. Choosing
02:28:25 out   a swatch changes every accent immediately: the brand mark, play icon, settings
02:28:25 out   highlights and folder highlights. Both choices are saved to
02:28:25 out   `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vidsync/settings.json` and restored on the next launch, so a
02:28:25 out   missing file simply means dark and purple.
02:28:25 out   ## Sources and unknowns
02:28:25 out   - The latest request removes the empty-stage prompt, the sample-clip shortcut
